  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Perched on the heights of Grimaud (592 chemin des Mûres), La Baie des Voiles is the restaurant of the Château Rose hotel, with a view over the Gulf of Saint-Tropez. The tourist office tells the story of the place: formerly the home of Senator Louis Sigallas and then of the actor and playwright Sacha Guitry, the Château Rose has become an 18-room hotel, with "instinctive and seasonal" cuisine by the starred chef Christophe Chiavola. The restaurant has a dining room; the tourist office page mentions a menu from 30 €, a car park, a lift and air conditioning. A cocktail bar with a panoramic terrace, the Bar Saint-Germain, is open in the same hotel.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's page on the Golfe de Saint-Tropez Destination website, fed by the Grimaud tourist office, says "Pets accepted". It does not specify the dining room or the terrace, the dog's size, or any supplement.</p>
      <p>As for hours, the same page announces an opening period from 2 November 2026 to 3 January 2027: Wednesday to Sunday from 8am to 2:30pm and from 7:30pm to 10:30pm, closed Monday and Tuesday. After 3 January 2027, call 04 94 82 65 70.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: mention that you are coming with your dog when you book and ask whether it can stay close to you in the dining room.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant overlooks the Gulf of Saint-Tropez, on the outskirts of Grimaud: plan to drive up, the hotel car park is mentioned on the tourist office page. For walks with your dog in the town, see the Grimaud tourist office website.</p>
    </div>

